two pointer approach is a common technique is using two pointers to 
traverse the data structure, either from difference ends of the array or the same end with different speeds
this can help to reduce the time complexity.

Mostly we can classify these problems into three variations

fixed window so the two pointers are used to maintain a window of a certain size
we slide the window across the array to find the desired result. 
This is often used in problems involving subarrays or substrings of whose length is k 
and we want to find the maximum, minimum, or sum of elements in that window.


pointers at opposite ends of the array, this is often used in problems 
where we need to find pairs of elements that satisfy a certain condition.

slow and fast pointer, this is often used in problems where we need to 
find a cycle in a linked list or an array.